// sptape.ac -- the tape module: a picture's save to and load from the Type 550 Microtape on
// the drive in use, and the tape's directory, which the keyboard service shows as the
// directory's screen, on which Save and Load pick one of the twelve pictures.
//
// Bank 11, after the overlay manager. The root part comes first: the words the module keeps
// between calls, the name Save writes, the directory, Save's keyboard block with its prompts, and
// the directory's screen's blocks and the masters' picker's, which the keyboard service reads
// (spkbd.ac, kbOpen) through their 16-bit addresses, the screens themselves being the overlay
// kbd's (dirList, its lines written from tpDir at the open). Then the overlay tape, read
// into the window W, in bank 6, from the drum when it is called (Docs/UsingOverlays.md): Save,
// Load, Dir and their helpers, the run lists, and the words used within one call; it reaches
// the root's words through their 16-bit addresses. Then, in the root again, the tape's
// primitives (mount, seek, read and write), which the overlays tape and library both call.
// Then the two root stubs, tapeEntry, from the main bank's tapeCall, and tpPickName, from
// tapeStep, each calling the overlay's entry of its name with Ov added; tapeEntry passes the
// library's entries to the library's stub (splib.ac). Last tapeStep, the steps of Misc's Save,
// Load and Dir rows, for the main bank's actTape, which passes Library's rows to the library's
// libStep (splib.ac). The
// module runs with the extend window open throughout, so every indirect address is a 16-bit
// one, and calls nothing outside W and bank 11 but the view module's vwInit (bank 12).
// Part of sketchpad.am1, included where it stands.
//
// The tape's layout, format 21; no other is read (sketchpad.ah, TPFORMAT). Picture p (0
// to 11, P1 to P12) has a slot of TPSLOT blocks, P1 to P6 from block 1, P7 to P12 from
// TPDIRBLK + 1 (tpFirst); block TPDIRBLK between them is the tape's directory, and block 0 is
// not used. A picture is three parts, one after another from
// its slot's first block. First the stream, TPPBLOCKS blocks, its runs in tpSaveRuns' order: the
// header (tpHdr, holding the magic, the format, TPSTREAM, a generation word, new for each save
// from the clock, and the entries' blocks), the constraint table, the tie lists packed two to a
// word (tpPack), the name, the cycle's settings packed (tpCyPk), the masters' constraints'
// counts, the texts, the digits, the picture's runs (TPPICTURE) and the masters' nesting (mNSub
// to mTxOwn), then zeros. Then the masters' entries, one for each master with words, M1's first,
// each from a block's start: its record's tables as far as the directory's counts (tpRecT, an
// empty one left out, its sub-instances last), then its name, its line's run on the masters'
// picker, then zeros to its last block's end. Last the closing block, zeros, then the header
// again as its last words. A save writes them forward, so one cut short leaves the two headers
// unlike and the picture reads as empty (the scheme of the Z-machine interpreter's zsave.ac). A
// never-written
// block reads as zeros and passes its checksum, so the magic is what marks a picture; a picture
// of any other format reads as empty too, and so does one whose entries would run past its
// slot. A save refuses, TOO BIG, a picture whose entries would, before it writes anything. The
// directory block holds the magic, the format, TPDIRW and two zeros, then the twelve entries of
// tpDir, each the picture's format word and its name's run. A save writes it after the picture,
// with the picture's entry, so one cut short between the two leaves the directory naming the old
// picture. A load judges a picture by its headers alone. A directory whose sum fails is refused,
// BAD BLOCK, and a library tape's (splib.ac), NOT PICT, by every command. One of another format
// reads as twelve empty entries, and so does a block that is not Sketchpad's at all: all zeros,
// a blank tape, or another program's words, which a save then refuses, NOT BLANK, writing
// nothing. A save onto a blank directory first reads every block it will write, and refuses the
// same way unless all are zeros or the first holds a picture's magic (tpScan), since another
// program may have left the directory's block alone and used the slot's (the Z-machine's saves
// start at block 1).
//
// The transfer. The tape gives or wants a word every 200 us and does not wait, so the break
// system is off while it runs and the display shows WAIT from waitList, a list that loops on
// itself (tapeCall turns the breaks and the frame back on). Every wait polls mrs, as zsave.ac's
// loops do; a halt clears GO with no error, so a wait for a word also tests GO. A save reads the
// directory again, writes the stream, each entry and the closing block, then the directory. A
// load reads the picture's first block for its header, then all its blocks forward once,
// keeping only the two headers and checking every block's sum, so a picture that fails leaves
// the drawing as it was; then turns and reads the stream in reverse, a block's words last first
// (Docs/UsingType550Microtape.md), straight into the tables, walking the runs backward
// (tpLoadRuns); then each entry forward into its master's record, and the master's words into
// the master store at the place the save found them there (mStart), if it was in it. A pass that
// fails once the tables have begun to change leaves them empty.
//
// A master's record is made resident only by the root (mrLoad, spinst.ac), never while an
// overlay's entry runs, so the entries go one call each: the overlay returns TSMORE with tpK the
// master, and the root stub tapeEntry makes its record resident and calls the overlay again with
// TEMORE, which transfers the entry and finds the next master. The tape is stopped while the
// drum turns. The words an operation keeps across those calls, tpHdr, tpOp, tpK, tpKN and
// tpBlkN, are the root's.

// The module's constants, the picture's format, words and blocks, the directory's and the waits,
// are in sketchpad.ah, the tape module's group.

// A run list's entry, three words: the run's first word, its count complemented (the word loops
// take the next run inline, so they do no cma), and its step. A run of
// n words from first, forward; the same run from its last word back, step -1, for the reverse
// pass; and n words to or from tpZero or tpSink, step 0.
#define TPRUN(first, n) first; 0 - (n); 1
#define TPREV(first, n) first + (n) - 1; 0 - (n); 0 - 1
#define TPZEROS(n) tpZero:6; 0 - (n); 0
#define TPSINK(n) tpSink:6; 0 - (n); 0

// The runs of a picture's words, one stream, and the same runs backward for the reverse pass, in
// the reverse order. lineCount and pointCount are a var pair, allocated downward. The masters'
// attachers (cpAtt to cpNAtt), the master directory, the instance table and the arc table are
// four runs, one after another in the stream. The master store is not in it: a load puts each
// master's words back from its entry (tpPool).
#define TPPICTURE \
    TPRUN(pointX:3, MAXPTS); \
    TPRUN(pointY:3, MAXPTS); \
    TPRUN(lineFrom:3, 2 * MAXLINES); \
    TPRUN(iX:3, MAXINST); \
    TPRUN(iY:3, MAXINST); \
    TPRUN(iScale:3, MAXINST); \
    TPRUN(cpAtt:5, TPATTWORDS); \
    TPRUN(mLen:5, TPMDIRWORDS); \
    TPRUN(instCount:012, TPINSTWORDS); \
    TPRUN(arcCount:2, TPARCWORDS); \
    TPRUN(lineCount:4, 2)
#define TPPICTREV \
    TPREV(lineCount:4, 2); \
    TPREV(arcCount:2, TPARCWORDS); \
    TPREV(instCount:012, TPINSTWORDS); \
    TPREV(mLen:5, TPMDIRWORDS); \
    TPREV(cpAtt:5, TPATTWORDS); \
    TPREV(iScale:3, MAXINST); \
    TPREV(iY:3, MAXINST); \
    TPREV(iX:3, MAXINST); \
    TPREV(lineFrom:3, 2 * MAXLINES); \
    TPREV(pointY:3, MAXPTS); \
    TPREV(pointX:3, MAXPTS)

// The runs of the texts' words: the text module's in bank 10 from txN, the counts, each master's
// texts' cost and the canvas's texts; then the masters' texts in bank 11 from mtM; TPTWORDS in
// all. Two long runs, not a run a table, since short runs in a row leave a word loop too little
// time.
#define TPTEXTS \
    TPRUN(txN:012, TPTWCAN); \
    TPRUN(mtM:013, TPTWMAS)
#define TPTEXTREV \
    TPREV(mtM:013, TPTWMAS); \
    TPREV(txN:012, TPTWCAN)

// The runs of the digits' words: bank 3's, each canvas text's anchor and scalar, the scalars'
// count, values and fixes; then the text module's, each master's text's anchor, value and fix.
// Two long runs.
#define TPDIGITS \
    TPRUN(txAn:3, TPSCAN); \
    TPRUN(mtAn:013, TPSMAS)
#define TPDIGREV \
    TPREV(mtAn:013, TPSMAS); \
    TPREV(txAn:3, TPSCAN)

// The directory's screen is the keyboard's (spkbd.ac, dirList), its lines sketchpad.ah's
// DIRLINE, which the library's screen and the masters' picker share.

// The module's words kept between calls.
tpName,                 // the name a save writes, typed on the keyboard (tpSvBlk)
    table NAMEW - 1, KBPAD
    KBBLANK
tpDir,                  // the tape's directory, each picture's entry its format word and name
    table TPDIRW, 0
tpHdr,                  // a save's header, written again in its closing block
    table TPHDRWORDS, 0
tpOp, 0                 // the operation under way across its entries' calls, TESAVE or TELOAD
tpK, 0                  // the master whose entry is next, its record made resident by the root
tpKN, 0                 // the master after it, the next one looked at
tpBlkN, 0               // the block the next entry, or the closing block, starts at

// Save's keyboard block (spkbd.ac, kbOpen). It holds the text keyboard, NAMELEN characters,
// the prompt tpPickNameOv sets from tpPrmT (one of tpPrm1 to tpPrm12, below), the name's run as
// the buffer, the main bank's resume, and the run's codes.
tpSvBlk, KBTEXT
    NAMELEN
    0
    tpName:013
    tapeResume:4
    NAMEWC
tpPrm1, type340 "P1 name"
tpPrm2, type340 "P2 name"
tpPrm3, type340 "P3 name"
tpPrm4, type340 "P4 name"
tpPrm5, type340 "P5 name"
tpPrm6, type340 "P6 name"
tpPrm7, type340 "P7 name"
tpPrm8, type340 "P8 name"
tpPrm9, type340 "P9 name"
tpPrm10, type340 "P10 name"
tpPrm11, type340 "P11 name"
tpPrm12, type340 "P12 name"

// The directory's screen's blocks, Dir's, Save's and Load's, which tapeStep gives the main
// bank's actTape. Each holds the kind, KBDIR; the keys
// the screen acts on, its key alone for Dir, and for the picker its key, Cancel, and the twelve
// lines; the key's text, three words, which kbOpen copies into dirKTxt; the screen's number,
// KBSDIR, in the buffer's place; the resume; and no run. The screen itself, its tables and the
// writing of its lines from tpDir are the keyboard's (spkbd.ac, dirList and kbDirFill).
tpDirBlk, KBDIR
    1
    tpOKTxt:013
    KBSDIR
    nothing:4
    0
tpSvPick, KBDIR
    DIRKEYS
    tpCanTxt:013
    KBSDIR
    tapeResume:4
    0
tpLdPick, KBDIR
    DIRKEYS
    tpCanTxt:013
    KBSDIR
    tapeResume:4
    0
tpOKTxt,
    017 * 010000 + 013 * 0100 + KCUP
    KBPAD
    KBBLANK
tpCanTxt,
    003 * 010000 + KCLOW * 0100 + 001
    016 * 010000 + 003 * 0100 + 005
    014 * 010000 + KCUP * 0100 + KCEND

// The masters' picker: the directory's screen made again for the masters (the keyboard's KBDIR
// screens, spkbd.ac), its list and lines in bank 5 (sketchpad.am1's mpkList), its blocks and
// its lines' addresses here, its descriptor, codes and hit records the keyboard's.

// The picker's blocks, Define's, Inst's, Copy's, Change's (its Master row) and Dwell's, which
// the instance module's instKbOpen gives the main bank's actKb, and Library's Save's and Load's,
// which it gives libStep (splib.ac). Each holds the kind, KBDIR; its keys, Cancel and the
// sixteen lines; Cancel's text; the screen's number, KBSMPK; and the resume, the row's
// action, which takes the master picked (pkTake), or for Dwell and Define ckDone, which opens
// Dwell's number keyboard or Define's name keyboard (instKbDone), or for Library's rows the
// main bank's tapeResume.
mpkDfBlk, KBDIR
    MPKEYS
    tpCanTxt:013
    KBSMPK
    ckDone:4
    0
mpkInBlk, KBDIR
    MPKEYS
    tpCanTxt:013
    KBSMPK
    actInst:4
    0
mpkCpBlk, KBDIR
    MPKEYS
    tpCanTxt:013
    KBSMPK
    actCopy:4
    0
mpkChBlk, KBDIR
    MPKEYS
    tpCanTxt:013
    KBSMPK
    actChange:4
    0
mpkDwBlk, KBDIR
    MPKEYS
    tpCanTxt:013
    KBSMPK
    ckDone:4
    0
mpkLsBlk, KBDIR
    MPKEYS
    tpCanTxt:013
    KBSMPK
    tapeResume:4
    0
mpkLlBlk, KBDIR
    MPKEYS
    tpCanTxt:013
    KBSMPK
    tapeResume:4
    0

// The picker's keys' parameter words' addresses: Cancel's first, then the lines', M1 to M16,
// which the tape, the library and the instance module read too, to reach a master's line.
mpkBlkT,
    mpkKey:5
    mpkL:5 + 0 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 1 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 2 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 3 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 4 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 5 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 6 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 7 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 0d8 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 0d9 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 0d10 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 0d11 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 0d12 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 0d13 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 0d14 * MPKWORDS
    mpkL:5 + 0d15 * MPKWORDS

// The overlay tape: Save, Load and Dir (tapeEntryOv) and Save's name (tpPickNameOv), with every
// word they use within one call, read again from the drum at each load.
%%overlay tape, W
    export tapeEntryOv, tpPickNameOv

// The words the overlay's copies and walks use within one call: tpMove's source, tpPtr, and
// destination, tpRun, each a 16-bit pointer, and a walk's count, tpCnt.
tpRun, 0
tpPtr, 0
tpCnt, 0

// Run entry n, TESAVE to TEMORE, on picture tapePic of drive tapeDrive. The break system is
// turned off first and the display set to WAIT (waitList), off the frame; the tape is stopped
// at the end, whatever happened. TEMORE goes on with a save or a load, the drive already
// selected, once the root has made master tpK's record resident.
// Entry: IO = n; AC = the return address, which carries the main bank. Exit: AC = the result,
// TSSAVED to TSTOOBIG, the window open, the display showing WAIT and the break system off; or
// TSMORE, for master tpK's record, with no word set for the status. IO is clobbered. Called
// through the root stub tapeEntry, by the manager.
tapeEntryOv,
    local teRtn, teSel, teRes, teJmp, teTab, teStop, teCopy, teNm1, teNm2, teNm3, tePtr, teTo, \
        teN, teGo
    dac teRtn
    dio teSel
    lsm
    lio [waitList:1]
    dla
    lac teSel
    sad [TEMORE]        // skip unless an entry's turn, the drive selected
    jmp teGo
    jsp i [tpMount:013]
    sza                 // skip if the drive has a tape
    jmp teStop
teGo,
    lac teSel
    add [teTab]
    dap teJmp
teJmp, jsp .            // the entry's routine, by a jump table, returns here
    jmp teStop
teTab,
    jmp tpSave          // TESAVE
    jmp tpLoad          // TELOAD
    jmp tpGetDir        // TEDIR
    jmp tpMore          // TEMORE
teStop,
    dac teRes
    cli
    mlc                 // stop, since a moving tape runs off its reel
    lac teRes
    sad [TSMORE]        // skip unless the root is to make a record resident
    jmp i teRtn

    // The status word's text for the result, while the display shows WAIT.
    lac teRes
    sal 2s
    add [tpMsgs:6]
    dac tePtr
    lac [msgText:0]
    dac teTo
    lac [0-4]
    dac teN
teCopy,
    lac i tePtr
    dac i teTo
    idx tePtr
    idx teTo
    isp teN
    jmp teCopy

    // And the name's line under it, the name saved or loaded, blank after any other result.
    lac teRes
    sas [TSSAVED]       // skip if saved
    jmp teNm1
    lac [tpName:013]
    jmp teNm3
teNm1,
    sas [TSLOADED]      // skip if loaded
    jmp teNm2
    lac [tpNameR:6]
    jmp teNm3
teNm2,
    lac [tpBlank:6]
teNm3,
    dac tpPtr
    lac [msgName:0]
    dac tpRun
    law NAMEW
    jda tpMove
    lac teRes
    jmp i teRtn
teRtn, 0
teSel, 0
teRes, 0
tePtr, 0
teTo, 0
teN, 0
    endloc

// The status word's texts, four words each, by the result, TSSAVED to TSOTHER. Nine characters
// each, padded with spaces (spframe.ac, msgWord). A load that failed after it began replacing
// the tables reads BAD BLOCK, as a bad block does. TSOPEN's is never shown (tapeCall), nor are
// TSMORE's, the library's TSLLOADED to TSNOTLIB, nor any from TSFULL to TSDIGIT, the library's and
// Plot's, which only hold their places, as zeros from TSFULL on.
tpMsgs,
    type340 "SAVED    "
    type340 "LOADED   "
    type340 "NO TAPE  "
    type340 "LOCKED   "
    type340 "EMPTY    "
    type340 "BAD BLOCK"
    type340 "NO FLAG  "
    type340 "BAD BLOCK"
    type340 "         "
    type340 "TOO BIG  "
    type340 "         "
    type340 "         "
    type340 "         "
    type340 "         "
    type340 "NOT PICT "
    table 4 * (TSOTHER - TSNOTPIC - 1), 0
    type340 "NOT BLANK"

// A blank name's run (NAMEW words, sketchpad.ah), which the keyboard reads as an empty text.
tpBlank,
    table NAMEW - 1, KBPAD
    KBBLANK

// The first block of picture tapePic, from tpFirst.
// Exit: AC = the block. IO is preserved. Called via jsp.
tpBase,
    local rtn, tbP
    dap rtn
    lac i [tapePic:4]
    add [tpFirst:6]
    dac tbP
    lac i tbP
rtn, jmp .
tbP, 0
    endloc

// Picture tapePic's entry in the directory, from tpEntT.
// Exit: AC = the entry's 16-bit address. IO is preserved. Called via jsp.
tpEntry,
    local rtn, tyP
    dap rtn
    lac i [tapePic:4]
    add [tpEntT:6]
    dac tyP
    lac i tyP
rtn, jmp .
tyP, 0
    endloc

// Save the picture: its stream, here, then each master's entry (tpMore) and the closing block
// and the directory (tpSvEnd). The entries' blocks counted first (tpEnts), and a picture they
// would carry past its slot refused, before anything is written; a new generation in the
// header; the directory read again, since the tape may have changed since the picker read it,
// and another program's refused (tpOther); on a blank directory (tpDirZ), every block the save
// will write read first, the stream's, the entries' and the closing one, and refused unless all
// are zeros or the first holds a picture's magic (tpScan); the seek to the picture's first block
// and the stream's TPPBLOCKS blocks written; then the first master's entry asked for (tpNext).
// Exit: AC = the result, TSMORE, TSTOOBIG, TSOTHER, or tpRdDir's, tpSeek's, tpScan's or
// tpWrite's failure, or tpNext's. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpSave,
    local rtn, tsBig, tsGo, tsNot
    dap rtn
    jsp tpEnts
    dac i [tpHdr:013+4]
    add [TPPBLOCKS - TPSLOT]
    sma                 // skip if the entries and the closing block fit the slot
    jmp tsBig
    lac [TPMAGIC]
    dac i [tpHdr:013]
    lac [TPFORMAT]
    dac i [tpHdr:013+1]
    lac [TPSTREAM]
    dac i [tpHdr:013+2]
    rck
    dio i [tpHdr:013+3] // the generation
    jsp tpPack
    jsp tpCyPk
    jsp tpRdDir
    sza                 // skip if the directory was read
    jmp rtn
    lac tpOther
    sza                 // skip unless another program's tape
    jmp tsNot
    lac tpDirZ
    sza i               // skip if a blank directory, to read the blocks first
    jmp tsGo
    lac i [tpHdr:013+4]
    add [TPPBLOCKS + 1]
    cma
    dac tpScB           // minus the blocks the save writes
    jsp tpBase
    dac i [tpWant:013]
    dzm i [tpRev:013]
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the picture's first block
    jmp rtn
    jsp tpScan
    sza                 // skip if read
    jmp rtn
    lac tpW0
    sad [TPMAGIC]       // skip unless a picture's first block
    jmp tsGo
    lac tpOr
    sza                 // skip if every word was zero
    jmp tsNot
tsGo,
    jsp tpBase
    dac i [tpWant:013]
    dzm i [tpRev:013]
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the picture's first block
    jmp rtn
    lac [tpSaveRuns:6]
    dac i [tpList:013]
    law i TPPBLOCKS
    dac i [tpBlk:013]
    jsp i [tpWrite:013]
    sza                 // skip if written
    jmp rtn
    jsp tpBase
    add [TPPBLOCKS]
    dac i [tpBlkN:013]
    dzm i [tpOp:013]    // TESAVE
    dzm i [tpKN:013]
    jsp tpNext
    jmp rtn
tsNot,
    law TSOTHER
    jmp rtn
tsBig,
    lac [TSTOOBIG]
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// A save's close, every entry written: the closing block, at tpBlkN; then the picture's entry in
// the directory, its format and the name typed, and the directory written.
// Exit: AC = the result, 0 (TSSAVED), or tpSeek's or tpWrite's failure. IO is clobbered. Called
// via jsp.
tpSvEnd,
    local rtn
    dap rtn
    lac i [tpBlkN:013]
    dac i [tpWant:013]
    dzm i [tpRev:013]
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the closing block
    jmp rtn
    lac [tpTrlRuns:6]
    dac i [tpList:013]
    law i 1
    dac i [tpBlk:013]
    jsp i [tpWrite:013]
    sza                 // skip if written
    jmp rtn
    jsp tpEntry
    dac tpRun
    lac [TPFORMAT]
    dac i tpRun
    idx tpRun
    lac [tpName:013]
    dac tpPtr
    law NAMEW
    jda tpMove
    lac [TPDIRBLK]
    dac i [tpWant:013]
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the directory's block
    jmp rtn
    lac [tpDirWRuns:6]
    dac i [tpList:013]
    law i 1
    dac i [tpBlk:013]
    jsp i [tpWrite:013]
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// Read the tape's directory block into tpDir, the rest of the block after it into tpEBuf. A
// block whose sum is not zero is refused, BAD BLOCK, since the pictures behind it may still be
// read; a library tape's directory (splib.ac), NOT PICT, so that no save writes over it. A
// picture tape's directory of another format than this one reads as twelve empty
// entries, as does a block with neither magic: tpDirZ set when every word of it is zero, a
// blank tape, and tpOther when not, another program's, which a save refuses (tpSave). That is
// not a failure, so that Dir and Load show the empty entries.
// Exit: AC = 0, TSBAD, TSNOTPIC, or tpSeek's or tpRead's failure; tpDirZ and tpOther set. IO is
// clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpRdDir,
    local rtn, trdNone, trdLoop, trdSum, trdLib, trdTest, trdOther
    dap rtn
    dzm tpDirZ
    dzm tpOther
    lac [TPDIRBLK]
    dac i [tpWant:013]
    dzm i [tpRev:013]
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the directory's block
    jmp rtn
    lac [tpDirRRuns:6]
    dac i [tpList:013]
    law i 1
    dac i [tpBlk:013]
    jsp i [tpRead:013]
    sza                 // skip unless a tape error
    jmp rtn
    lac i [tpBad:013]
    sza i               // skip if the block's sum failed
    jmp trdSum
    lac [TSBAD]
    jmp rtn
trdSum,
    lac tpHdrB
    sas [LBMAGIC]       // skip if a library tape's directory
    jmp trdLib
    lac [TSNOTPIC]
    jmp rtn
trdLib,
    sas [TPMAGIC]       // skip if the magic
    jmp trdTest
    lac tpHdrB+1
    sas [TPFORMAT]      // skip if this format
    jmp trdNone
    lac tpHdrB+2
    sas [TPDIRW]        // skip if a directory, not a picture
    jmp trdNone
    cla
    jmp rtn
trdTest,                // neither magic: a blank tape or another program's
    dzm tpOr
    law i TPHDRWORDS
    dac tpCnt
    lac [tpHdrB:6]
    jda tpOrN
    law i TPDIRW
    dac tpCnt
    lac [tpDir:013]
    jda tpOrN
    law i TPDIRREST
    dac tpCnt
    lac [tpEBuf:6]
    jda tpOrN
    lac tpOr
    sza                 // skip if every word is zero, a blank tape
    jmp trdOther
    idx tpDirZ
    jmp trdNone
trdOther,
    idx tpOther
trdNone,
    lac [tpDir:013]
    dac tpPtr
    law i NPICT
    dac tpCnt
trdLoop,
    dzm i tpPtr         // the entry's format word, no picture
    lac tpPtr
    add [TPDENT]
    dac tpPtr
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every entry is emptied
    jmp trdLoop
    cla
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// The OR of -tpCnt words from a 16-bit address into tpOr, which the caller clears first.
// Entry: AC = the first word's address. Exit: AC = tpOr. IO is preserved. Called via jda.
tpOrN, 0
    local rtn, onLoop
    dap rtn
    lac tpOrN
    dac tpPtr
onLoop,
    lac i tpPtr
    ior tpOr
    dac tpOr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every word is taken
    jmp onLoop
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// Read -tpScB blocks forward and keep none of their words, the seek having just found the
// first block's flag: every data word ORed into tpOr, and the first block's first kept in tpW0.
// Not the checksums, since a block never written gives a leading one of minus zero; no sum is
// checked, since only zeros matter. A loop of its own, since tpRead's has no time for the OR at
// a run change. The tape is stopped after the last.
// Exit: AC = 0; TSBAD on a tape error. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpScan,
    local rtn, scBlock, scData, scNoDF, scBEF, scErr, scK, scW
    dap rtn
    lio [mtgo mtread]
    mlc
    dzm tpOr
    dzm tpW0
    law i 1
    dac scW             // the first data word
scBlock,
    law i 2
    dac scK             // the block's leading checksum, then its data
scData,
    mrs
    spi i               // skip if the data flag is up
    jmp scNoDF
    mrd
    isp scK             // skip past the leading checksum
    jmp scData
    lai
    ior tpOr
    dac tpOr
    isp scW             // skip at the first block's first data word
    jmp scData
    dio tpW0
    lac [0400000]       // and never again: more words than any tape holds
    dac scW
    jmp scData
scNoDF,
    ril 1s              // the block end flag to bit 0
    spi
    jmp scBEF
    ril 1s              // the error flag to bit 0
    spi
    jmp scErr
    ril 4s              // GO (bit 6) to bit 0, clear after a halt
    spi
    jmp scData
    jmp scErr
scBEF,
    mrd                 // the trailing checksum
    isp tpScB           // skip after the last block
    jmp scBlock
    mrs
    dio tpScSt
    cli
    mlc                 // stop
    lac tpScSt
    and [mterf]
    sza i               // skip if a tape error
    jmp rtn             // AC = 0
scErr,
    cli
    mlc                 // stop
    lac [TSBAD]
rtn, jmp .
scK, 0
scW, 0
    endloc

// Load the picture: its stream, here, then each master's entry (tpMore) and the close
// (tpLdEnd). The picture's first block read alone, for its header, which must hold the magic,
// this format and its stream's size, and entries that end within the slot; then the check pass
// over all its blocks, keeping only the two headers; the headers judged, then the blocks' sums;
// then the reverse search to the stream's last block, and the reverse pass into the tables
// (tpLoadRuns); the entries' blocks counted from the tables just read, which must be the
// header's; the masters' texts' costs within MTBUDGET and each pool's top within the pool, as
// every save leaves them (the text module's txFit); the instances within MAXINST and each one's
// master within NMASTER; then the first master's entry asked for (tpNext). A pass that fails
// once the tables have begun to change empties them (tpWipe).
// Exit: AC = the result, TSMORE, TSEMPTY, TSBAD, TSWIPED, or tpSeek's or tpRead's failure, or
// tpNext's. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpLoad,
    local rtn, tlFirst, tlN, tlK, tlEmpty, tlBad, tlWipe, tlCost, tlMast, tlNew
    dap rtn
    jsp tpBase
    dac tlFirst
    dac i [tpWant:013]
    dzm i [tpRev:013]
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the picture's first block
    jmp rtn
    lac [tpHdRuns:6]
    dac i [tpList:013]
    law i 1
    dac i [tpBlk:013]
    jsp i [tpRead:013]
    sza                 // skip unless a tape error
    jmp rtn
    lac i [tpBad:013]
    sza                 // skip if the block's sum was zero
    jmp tlBad
    lac tpHdrA
    sas [TPMAGIC]       // skip if a picture
    jmp tlEmpty
    lac tpHdrA+1
    sas [TPFORMAT]      // skip if this format
    jmp tlEmpty
    lac [TPSTREAM]
    sas tpHdrA+2        // skip if its size
    jmp tlEmpty
    lac tpHdrA+4
    add [TPPBLOCKS - TPSLOT]
    sma                 // skip if the entries and the closing block end within the slot
    jmp tlEmpty

    // The check pass, the picture's tlN blocks from its first: the stream, the entries and the
    // closing block, every word but the two headers to tpSink (tpChkN).
    lac tpHdrA+4
    add [TPPBLOCKS + 1]
    dac tlN
    sal 8s              // its words
    sub [2 * TPHDRWORDS]
    cma
    dac tpChkN
    lac tlFirst
    dac i [tpWant:013]
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the picture's first block
    jmp rtn
    lac [tpCheckRuns:6]
    dac i [tpList:013]
    lac tlN
    cma
    dac i [tpBlk:013]
    jsp i [tpRead:013]
    sza                 // skip unless a tape error
    jmp rtn

    // The headers must be alike, the generation and the entries' blocks included.
    lac tpHdrA
    sas tpHdrB          // skip if the closing header agrees
    jmp tlEmpty
    lac tpHdrA+1
    sas tpHdrB+1
    jmp tlEmpty
    lac tpHdrA+2
    sas tpHdrB+2
    jmp tlEmpty
    lac tpHdrA+3
    sas tpHdrB+3
    jmp tlEmpty
    lac tpHdrA+4
    sas tpHdrB+4
    jmp tlEmpty
    lac i [tpBad:013]
    sza                 // skip if every block's sum was zero
    jmp tlBad

    // The reverse pass, from the stream's last block. Nothing has been changed until now.
    lac tlFirst
    add [TPPBLOCKS - 1]
    dac i [tpWant:013]
    law 1
    dac i [tpRev:013]
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the stream's last block, going back
    jmp rtn
    lac [tpLoadRuns:6]
    dac i [tpList:013]
    law i TPPBLOCKS
    dac i [tpBlk:013]
    jsp i [tpReadR:013]
    sza                 // skip unless a tape error
    jmp tlWipe
    lac i [tpBad:013]
    sza                 // skip if every block's sum was zero
    jmp tlWipe
    jsp tpEnts
    sas tpHdrA+4        // skip if the entries are the header's blocks
    jmp tlWipe
    lac [txMCost:012]
    dac tpPtr
    law i NMASTER
    dac tlK
    dzm tlN
tlCost,
    lac tlN
    add i tpPtr
    dac tlN
    idx tpPtr
    isp tlK             // skip once every master's cost is in
    jmp tlCost
    lac tlN
    sub [MTBUDGET+1]
    sma                 // skip unless past MTBUDGET
    jmp tlWipe
    lac i [txRS:012+NTEXT]
    sub [TXPOOLW+1]
    sma                 // skip unless past the canvas's pool
    jmp tlWipe
    lac i [mtRS:013+NMTEXT]
    sub [MTPOOLW+1]
    sma                 // skip unless past the masters' pool
    jmp tlWipe

    // The instances no more than MAXINST, and each one's master one of the NMASTER, as every
    // save leaves them: a master past them would send the rebuild's mrLoad (spinst.ac) past its
    // jump table, a hang. A sub gives -0 only for -0 - +0, so each bound is exact.
    lac i [instCount:012]
    spa                 // skip unless negative
    jmp tlWipe
    sub [MAXINST+1]
    sma                 // skip unless past MAXINST
    jmp tlWipe
    lac i [instCount:012]
    sza i               // skip if any instance
    jmp tlNew
    cma
    dac tlK
    lac [iMaster:012]
    dac tpPtr
tlMast,
    lac i tpPtr
    spa                 // skip unless negative
    jmp tlWipe
    sub [NMASTER]
    sma                 // skip if under NMASTER
    jmp tlWipe
    idx tpPtr
    isp tlK             // skip once every instance's master is in
    jmp tlMast
tlNew,
    lac tlFirst
    add [TPPBLOCKS]
    dac i [tpBlkN:013]
    law TELOAD
    dac i [tpOp:013]
    dzm i [tpKN:013]
    jsp tpNext
    jmp rtn
tlWipe,
    jsp tpWipe
    jmp rtn
tlEmpty,
    lac [TSEMPTY]
    jmp rtn
tlBad,
    lac [TSBAD]
rtn, jmp .
tlFirst, 0
tlN, 0
tlK, 0
    endloc

// A load's close, every entry read: each instance's scale k alone, its multiplier code dropped
// (TPKMASK); the cycle's settings and the ties unpacked; the name on the masters' picker of
// every master with no words blank, since the load replaced every master and wrote the others'
// from their entries; the main bank's rebuild readied.
// Exit: AC = TSLOADED. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpLdEnd,
    local rtn, tlScale, tlName, tlNext, tlK
    dap rtn
    dzm tlK
tlName,
    lac tlK
    add [mLen:5]
    dac tpPtr
    lac i tpPtr
    sza                 // skip if the master has no words; else its name is its entry's
    jmp tlNext
    lac tlK
    add [mpkBlkT:013 + 1]
    dac tpPtr
    lac i tpPtr
    add [MPKTAG]
    dac tpRun
    lac [mpkBlank:7]
    dac tpPtr
    law NAMEW
    jda tpMove
tlNext,
    idx tlK
    sas [NMASTER]       // skip once every master is taken
    jmp tlName
    lac [iScale:3]
    dac tpPtr
    law i MAXINST
    dac tpCnt
tlScale,
    lac i tpPtr
    and [TPKMASK]
    dac i tpPtr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every scale is masked
    jmp tlScale
    jsp i [vaEmpty:2]
    jsp tpCyUn
    jsp tpUnpack
    jsp tpFresh
    lac [TSLOADED]
rtn, jmp .
tlK, 0
    endloc

// A load's tables, partly replaced, all emptied: the master directory and the masters' nesting,
// the instances and arcs with their counts, the line and point counts, the constraint table's
// count, the ties, the masters' constraints' counts, the texts and the digits. The instance table
// first, in bank 10; then the master directory, in bank 5, with the nesting (mNSub to mTxOwn)
// after it as one run, and the arc table, in bank 2 (sparcdata.ac). No master left, no record is
// read.
// Exit: AC = TSWIPED. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpWipe,
    local rtn, tlZeroI, tlZeroM, tlZero, tlNoTie
    dap rtn
    jsp tpNoX
    jsp tpNoText
    jsp tpNoDig
    lac [instCount:012]
    dac tpPtr
    law i TPINSTWORDS
    dac tpCnt
tlZeroI,
    dzm i tpPtr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt
    jmp tlZeroI
    lac [mLen:5]
    dac tpPtr
    lac [TPMDIRWORDS + TPNESTW]
    cma
    dac tpCnt
tlZeroM,
    dzm i tpPtr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt
    jmp tlZeroM
    lac [arcCount:2]
    dac tpPtr
    lac [TPARCWORDS]
    cma
    dac tpCnt
tlZero,
    dzm i tpPtr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt
    jmp tlZero
    dzm i [lineCount:4]
    dzm i [pointCount:4]
    dzm i [cCount:011]
    lac [tpTies:6]
    dac tpPtr
    law i TPTIES
    dac tpCnt
tlNoTie,
    dzm i tpPtr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every word is cleared
    jmp tlNoTie
    jsp tpUnpack        // no ties
    jsp tpFresh
    lac [TSWIPED]
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// The next master with words from tpKN on: it becomes tpK, for the root to make its record
// resident and call TEMORE. With none left, the operation's close, tpSvEnd or tpLdEnd.
// Exit: AC = TSMORE, or the close's result. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpNext,
    local rtn, nxLoop, nxEnd, nxSave, nxP
    dap rtn
nxLoop,
    lac i [tpKN:013]
    sad [NMASTER]       // skip unless every master has been looked at
    jmp nxEnd
    dac i [tpK:013]
    idx i [tpKN:013]
    lac i [tpK:013]
    add [mLen:5]
    dac nxP
    lac i nxP
    sza i               // skip if the master has words
    jmp nxLoop
    lac [TSMORE]
    jmp rtn
nxEnd,
    lac i [tpOp:013]
    sza i               // skip if a load
    jmp nxSave
    jsp tpLdEnd
    jmp rtn
nxSave,
    jsp tpSvEnd
rtn, jmp .
nxP, 0
    endloc

// Master tpK's entry, its record made resident by the root: the entry's runs (tpEntRuns), its
// tables gathered into tpEBuf for a save (tpECopy) and tpBlkN past its blocks, all before the
// seek to its first block, since the seek leaves 400 us to start the transfer; then its blocks
// written from tpEBuf, or read into it and scattered to the tables; a load's master's words
// then put into the master store (tpPool). Then the next master (tpNext). A load's failure here
// empties the tables (tpWipe).
// Exit: AC = the result, TSMORE, a save's tpSeek's or tpWrite's failure, TSWIPED, or tpNext's.
// IO is clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpMore,
    local rtn, tmSvErr, tmErr, tmSave, tmRes, tmBlks, tmBRtn
    dap rtn
    lac i [tpBlkN:013]
    dac i [tpWant:013]
    dzm i [tpRev:013]
    lac i [tpOp:013]
    sza i               // skip if a load
    jmp tmSave
    lac [tpSink:6]
    jda tpEntRuns
    dac i [tpBlk:013]
    jsp tmBlks
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the entry's first block
    jmp tmErr
    jsp i [tpRead:013]
    sza                 // skip unless a tape error
    jmp tmErr
    lac i [tpBad:013]
    sza                 // skip if every block's sum was zero
    jmp tmErr
    law 1
    jda tpECopy         // out of tpEBuf into the record's tables
    jsp tpPool
    jsp tpNext
    jmp rtn
tmSave,
    lac [tpZero:6]
    jda tpEntRuns
    dac i [tpBlk:013]
    cla
    jda tpECopy         // the record's tables into tpEBuf
    jsp tmBlks
    jsp i [tpSeek:013]
    sza                 // skip if at the entry's first block
    jmp tmErr
    jsp i [tpWrite:013]
    sza                 // skip if written
    jmp rtn
    jsp tpNext
    jmp rtn
tmErr,
    dac tmRes
    lac i [tpOp:013]
    sza i               // skip if a load
    jmp tmSvErr
    jsp tpWipe
    jmp rtn
tmSvErr,
    lac tmRes           // a save's failure, as it is
rtn, jmp .

// tpBlkN past the entry's -tpBlk blocks, and tpRun at its runs.
tmBlks,
    dap tmBRtn
    lac i [tpBlk:013]
    cma
    add i [tpBlkN:013]
    dac i [tpBlkN:013]
    lac [tpEBufL:6]
    dac i [tpList:013]
tmBRtn, jmp .
tmRes, 0
    endloc

// The runs of master tpK's entry. In tpEntL, its record's tables as far as the directory's
// counts (tpRecT), each table's count times its multiplier, an empty run left out, then its
// name's run from its line on the masters' picker, then a 0 for tpECopy, since no run's first
// word is 0. In tpEBufL, the tape's: the tables' words as one
// run from tpEBuf, since short runs in a row leave a word loop too little time; then the
// padding to the last block's end, from or to the word given, if there is any; then the
// closing run, one word from or to it.
// Entry: AC = the padding's word, tpZero for a save, tpSink for a load. Exit: AC = the entry's
// blocks, complemented. IO is clobbered. Called via jda.
tpEntRuns, 0
    local rtn, erLoop, erMul, erNone, erEnd, erT, erQ, erN, erW, erC, erS, erM
    dap rtn
    lac [tpRecT:6]
    dac erT
    lac [tpEntL:6]
    dac erQ
    dzm erW
    law i TPRECN
    dac erN
erLoop,
    lac i erT           // the table's first word
    dac i erQ
    idx erT
    lac i erT           // the table of counts, by master
    add i [tpK:013]
    dac erC
    lac i erC
    dac erC             // the count
    idx erT
    lac i erT           // the multiplier
    cma
    dac erM
    idx erT
    dzm erS
erMul,
    lac erS
    add erC
    dac erS
    isp erM             // skip once the count is taken the multiplier's times
    jmp erMul
    lac erS
    sza i               // skip if the run has words
    jmp erNone
    add erW
    dac erW
    idx erQ
    lac erS
    cma
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    law 1
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
erNone,
    isp erN             // skip once every table is taken
    jmp erLoop
    lac i [tpK:013]
    add [mpkBlkT:013 + 1]
    dac erC
    lac i erC           // the master's line
    add [MPKTAG]
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    law i NAMEW
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    law 1
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    law NAMEW
    add erW
    dac erW
    dzm i erQ           // the runs' end, for tpECopy

    // The tape's list: the tables' words from tpEBuf, erW of them.
    lac [tpEBufL:6]
    dac erQ
    lac [tpEBuf:6]
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    lac erW
    cma
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    law 1
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ

    // The padding, the words to the last block's end.
    lac erW
    and [0377]
    sza i               // skip unless the words end on a block's end
    jmp erEnd
    cma
    add [0d256]
    dac erS
    add erW
    dac erW
    lac tpEntRuns
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    lac erS
    cma
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    dzm i erQ
    idx erQ
erEnd,
    lac tpEntRuns       // the closing run
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    lac [0-1]
    dac i erQ
    idx erQ
    dzm i erQ
    lac erW
    sar 8s              // its blocks
    cma
rtn, jmp .
erT, 0
erQ, 0
erN, 0
erW, 0
erC, 0
erS, 0
erM, 0
    endloc

// Master tpK's entry's tables and name, tpEntL's runs (tpEntRuns), copied one after another
// into tpEBuf for a save, or out of it for a load.
// Entry: AC = 0 into tpEBuf, 1 out of it. AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jda.
tpECopy, 0
    local rtn, ecLoop, ecGo, ecSv, ecAt, ecQ, ecB, ecD
    dap rtn
    lac tpECopy
    dac ecD
    lac [tpEntL:6]
    dac ecQ
    lac [tpEBuf:6]
    dac ecB
ecLoop,
    lac i ecQ           // the table's first word, 0 past the last
    sza i               // skip unless every table is copied
    jmp rtn
    dac tpPtr
    lac ecB
    dac tpRun
    lac ecD
    sza i               // skip if a load's, out of tpEBuf
    jmp ecGo
    lac tpPtr
    lio tpRun
    dac tpRun
    dio tpPtr           // from tpEBuf to the table
ecGo,
    idx ecQ
    lac i ecQ           // the run's count, complemented
    cma
    jda tpMove
    lac ecD
    sza i               // skip if a load's, tpEBuf's place in tpPtr
    jmp ecSv
    lac tpPtr
    jmp ecAt
ecSv,
    lac tpRun
ecAt,
    dac ecB
    idx ecQ
    idx ecQ             // past the step, to the next run
    jmp ecLoop
rtn, jmp .
ecQ, 0
ecB, 0
ecD, 0
    endloc

// The blocks of every master's entry, for each master with words (tpEntRuns).
// Exit: AC = the blocks, tpK = NMASTER. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpEnts,
    local rtn, esLoop, esNext, esB, esP
    dap rtn
    dzm esB
    dzm i [tpK:013]
esLoop,
    lac i [tpK:013]
    add [mLen:5]
    dac esP
    lac i esP
    sza i               // skip if the master has words
    jmp esNext
    lac [tpZero:6]
    jda tpEntRuns
    cma
    add esB
    dac esB
esNext,
    idx i [tpK:013]
    sas [NMASTER]       // skip once every master is counted
    jmp esLoop
    lac esB
rtn, jmp .
esB, 0
esP, 0
    endloc

// A loaded master's words, from its record (mrWords), put into the master store at its place
// there when the save was made (mStart), as the instance module's msAddr places them; or left
// out, the master out of the store then (MNOPOOL). A place the store's regions no longer hold
// whole, saved by a build whose regions were larger, leaves the master out too, and the
// rebuild brings it in where it fits (spvar.ac's vaOf).
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpPool,
    local rtn, tpR0, tpTo, tpOut, tpQ, tpM, tpN
    dap rtn
    lac i [tpK:013]
    add [mLen:5]
    dac tpQ
    lac i tpQ
    dac tpN
    lac i [tpK:013]
    add [mStart:5]
    dac tpQ
    lac i tpQ
    sad [MNOPOOL]       // skip unless out of the store
    jmp rtn
    dac tpM
    sub [MPOOL0]
    spa                 // skip if in region 1
    jmp tpR0
    add tpN
    sub [MPOOL1 + 1]
    sma                 // skip if region 1 holds it whole
    jmp tpOut
    lac tpM
    sub [MPOOL0]
    add [mpool1:1]
    jmp tpTo
tpR0,
    add tpN
    sub [1]
    sma                 // skip if region 0 holds it whole
    jmp tpOut
    lac tpM
    add [masters:0]
tpTo,
    dac tpRun
    lac [mrWords:5]
    dac tpPtr
    lac tpN
    jda tpMove
    jmp rtn
tpOut,
    lac [MNOPOOL]
    dac i tpQ
rtn, jmp .
tpQ, 0
tpM, 0
tpN, 0
    endloc

// Copy n words from tpPtr to tpRun, both left past them.
// Entry: AC = n, at least 1. AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jda.
tpMove, 0
    local rtn, tvLoop
    dap rtn
    lac tpMove
    cma
    dac tpCnt
tvLoop,
    lac i tpPtr
    dac i tpRun
    idx tpPtr
    idx tpRun
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every word is copied
    jmp tvLoop
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// No masters' constraints, for a load that failed. Every master's count in cpNCon is zeroed.
// AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jsp.
tpNoX,
    local rtn, txLoop
    dap rtn
    lac [cpNCon:011]
    dac tpPtr
    law i NMASTER
    dac tpCnt
txLoop,
    dzm i tpPtr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every count is cleared
    jmp txLoop
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// No texts, for a load that failed. The text module's counts and each master's texts'
// cost are zeroed. The main bank's tapeRebuild has the module take them up.
// AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jsp.
tpNoText,
    local rtn, tnLoop
    dap rtn
    dzm i [txN:012]
    dzm i [mtN:012]
    lac [txMCost:012]
    dac tpPtr
    law i NMASTER
    dac tpCnt
tnLoop,
    dzm i tpPtr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every cost is cleared
    jmp tnLoop
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// No digits, for a load that failed. Bank 3's run from txAn and bank 11's from mtAn
// are filled with NOPOINT but for the scalars' count, 0, so every canvas text's and master's
// text's anchor is NOPOINT, every text plain, and no scalar is left. The words past a count are
// never read, so NOPOINT serves there too.
// AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jsp.
tpNoDig,
    local rtn, tdFill, tdLoop, tdRtn
    dap rtn
    lac [txAn:3]
    dac tpPtr
    law i TPSCAN
    dac tpCnt
    jsp tdFill
    dzm i [txAn:3+(2 * NTEXT)] // scN's word
    lac [mtAn:013]
    dac tpPtr
    law i TPSMAS
    dac tpCnt
    jsp tdFill
rtn, jmp .

// -tpCnt words from tpPtr filled with NOPOINT; tpCnt is set before the jsp, which leaves its
// return in AC.
tdFill,
    dap tdRtn
tdLoop,
    lac [NOPOINT]
    dac i tpPtr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every word is written
    jmp tdLoop
tdRtn, jmp .
    endloc

// Dir's, Save's and Load's read (TEDIR): the tape's directory read into tpDir (tpRdDir), from
// which the keyboard's open writes the directory's screen (spkbd.ac, kbDirFill).
// Exit: AC = TSOPEN, or tpRdDir's failure. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpGetDir,
    local rtn
    dap rtn
    jsp tpRdDir
    sza i               // skip unless read
    lac [TSOPEN]
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// Save's name for the picture picked (tapePic, set by tapeStep). It sets the
// directory's entry's name, if it holds a picture, as the keyboard's starting value in tpName,
// blank otherwise; and the keyboard's prompt for the picture, in tpSvBlk. No tape is read, since
// the picker has just read the directory.
// Entry: AC = the return address, which carries the main bank. AC and IO are clobbered. Called
// through the root stub tpPickName, by the manager.
tpPickNameOv,
    local tpkRtn, tpkBlank, tpkCopy
    dac tpkRtn
    jsp tpEntry
    dac tpPtr
    lac i tpPtr
    sas [TPFORMAT]      // skip if a picture
    jmp tpkBlank
    idx tpPtr           // its name
    jmp tpkCopy
tpkBlank,
    lac [tpBlank:6]
    dac tpPtr
tpkCopy,
    lac [tpName:013]
    dac tpRun
    law NAMEW
    jda tpMove
    lac i [tapePic:4]
    add [tpPrmT:6]
    dac tpPtr
    lac i tpPtr
    dac i [tpSvBlk:013 + 2]
    jmp i tpkRtn
tpkRtn, 0
    endloc

// The tie lists packed into tpTies for the stream, two ties to a word, the first in the high 9
// bits, each 0 for none (NOPOINT) and otherwise its point plus 1.
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpPack,
    local rtn, tkLoop, tkT, tkP
    dap rtn
    lac [iTie:3]
    dac tkT
    lac [tpTies:6]
    dac tkP
    law i TPTIES
    dac tpCnt
tkLoop,
    lac i tkT
    and [0777]
    add [1]
    and [0777]          // NOPOINT's 0777 plus 1 leaves 0
    ral 9s              // not sal, since point 255's 0400 would go into the sign bit
    dac i tkP
    idx tkT
    lac i tkT
    and [0777]
    add [1]
    and [0777]
    ior i tkP
    dac i tkP
    idx tkT
    idx tkP
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every word is packed
    jmp tkLoop
rtn, jmp .
tkT, 0
tkP, 0
    endloc

// The tie lists unpacked from tpTies (tpPack's packing).
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpUnpack,
    local rtn, tuLoop, tuT, tuP
    dap rtn
    lac [iTie:3]
    dac tuT
    lac [tpTies:6]
    dac tuP
    law i TPTIES
    dac tpCnt
tuLoop,
    lac i tuP
    sar 9s
    jda tpUnF
    dac i tuT
    idx tuT
    lac i tuP
    jda tpUnF
    dac i tuT
    idx tuT
    idx tuP
    isp tpCnt           // skip once every word is unpacked
    jmp tuLoop
rtn, jmp .
tuT, 0
tuP, 0
    endloc

// A tie from the low 9 bits of a, 0 for none (NOPOINT), otherwise the point plus 1.
// Entry: AC = a. Exit: AC = the tie. IO is preserved. Called via jda.
tpUnF, 0
    dap tufRtn
    lac tpUnF
    and [0777]
    add [0777]
    and [0777]          // the point, or 0777 for none
    sad [0777]          // skip unless none
    lac [NOPOINT]
tufRtn, jmp .

// The cycle's settings packed into tpCyc for the stream. The instance module's dwells and the
// sequence's length as they are, then its NSEQ masters, 0 to 15, four to a word, four bits each,
// the first in the high bits of the word's low 16.
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpCyPk,
    local rtn, cpRun, cpWord, cpEnt, cpP, cpQ, cpN, cpE
    dap rtn
    lac [cyDw:7]
    dac cpP
    lac [tpCyc:6]
    dac cpQ
    law i NMASTER+1
    dac cpN
cpRun,
    lac i cpP
    dac i cpQ
    idx cpP
    idx cpQ
    isp cpN             // skip once the dwells and the length are copied
    jmp cpRun
    lac [cySq:7]
    dac cpP
    law i TPSEQW
    dac cpN
cpWord,
    dzm i cpQ
    law i 4
    dac cpE
cpEnt,
    lac i cpQ
    ral 4s
    dac i cpQ
    lac i cpP
    and [017]
    ior i cpQ
    dac i cpQ
    idx cpP
    isp cpE             // skip once the word holds four
    jmp cpEnt
    idx cpQ
    isp cpN             // skip once every word is packed
    jmp cpWord
rtn, jmp .
cpP, 0
cpQ, 0
cpN, 0
cpE, 0
    endloc

// The cycle's settings from tpCyc (tpCyPk's packing), after a load.
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp.
tpCyUn,
    local rtn, cuRun, cuWord, cuEnt, cuP, cuQ, cuN, cuE, cuW
    dap rtn
    lac [cyDw:7]
    dac cuQ
    lac [tpCyc:6]
    dac cuP
    law i NMASTER+1
    dac cuN
cuRun,
    lac i cuP
    dac i cuQ
    idx cuP
    idx cuQ
    isp cuN             // skip once the dwells and the length are copied
    jmp cuRun

    // Each word's four masters, the last in its low four bits, written from the word's last
    // entry back.
    lac [cySq:7+3]
    dac cuQ
    law i TPSEQW
    dac cuN
cuWord,
    lac i cuP
    dac cuW
    law i 4
    dac cuE
cuEnt,
    lac cuW
    and [017]
    dac i cuQ
    lac cuW
    rar 4s
    dac cuW
    law i 1
    add cuQ
    dac cuQ
    isp cuE             // skip once the word's four are written
    jmp cuEnt
    idx cuP
    lac cuQ
    add [0d8]           // the next word's last entry
    dac cuQ
    isp cuN             // skip once every word is unpacked
    jmp cuWord
rtn, jmp .
cuP, 0
cuQ, 0
cuN, 0
cuE, 0
cuW, 0
    endloc

// Ready the main bank's rebuild after the tables changed (tapeRebuild). Every point is marked as
// moving and no point dragged, so that the arc module's drag entry rewrites every arc; and an
// empty drawing list shown, its end pair written into slot 0 directly, the display being off
// the frame (on WAIT), with dirty set, so the main loop's rebuildDisplay writes every slot, as
// init does; and the view is at x1, as at start.
// AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jsp.
tpFresh,
    local rtn, tfLoop
    dap rtn
    lac [ptMark:3]
    dac tpPtr
    lac [MAXPTS]
    cma
    dac tpCnt
tfLoop,
    law 1
    dac i tpPtr
    idx tpPtr
    isp tpCnt
    jmp tfLoop
    lac [NOPOINT]
    dac i [dragIdx:4]
    dzm i [shownCount:4]
    dzm i [staleN:4]
    dzm i [flipAt:0]
    lac [next(subroutine)]
    dac i [drawList:1]
    lac [jump arcList:0 next(parameter)]
    dac i [drawList:1+1]
    jsp i [vwInit:014]  // the view at x1
    law 1
    dac i [dirty:4]
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// The run lists, each ended by a run never reached. A save's stream, and its closing block; a
// load's first block, its header kept; the check pass's, the two headers kept and every other
// word to tpSink, as many as tpLoad sets in tpChkN; the reverse pass's, the stream's runs
// backward in the reverse order, the header to tpSink; and the directory block's, read and
// written. An entry's is
// built in tpEntL (tpEntRuns).
tpSaveRuns,
    TPRUN(tpHdr:013, TPHDRWORDS)
    TPRUN(conTab:011, CONWORDS)
    TPRUN(tpTies:6, TPTIES)
    TPRUN(tpName:013, NAMEW)
    TPRUN(tpCyc:6, TPCYC)
    TPRUN(cpNCon:011, NMASTER)
    TPTEXTS
    TPDIGITS
    TPPICTURE
    TPRUN(mNSub:5, TPNESTW)
    TPZEROS(TPPAD)
    TPZEROS(1)
tpTrlRuns,
    TPZEROS(0d256 - TPHDRWORDS)
    TPRUN(tpHdr:013, TPHDRWORDS)
    TPZEROS(1)
tpHdRuns,
    TPRUN(tpHdrA:6, TPHDRWORDS)
    TPSINK(0d256 - TPHDRWORDS)
    TPSINK(1)
tpCheckRuns,
    TPRUN(tpHdrA:6, TPHDRWORDS)
    tpSink:6
tpChkN, 0               // the words between the headers, complemented
    0
    TPRUN(tpHdrB:6, TPHDRWORDS)
    TPSINK(1)
tpLoadRuns,
    TPSINK(TPPAD)
    TPREV(mNSub:5, TPNESTW)
    TPPICTREV
    TPDIGREV
    TPTEXTREV
    TPREV(cpNCon:011, NMASTER)
    TPREV(tpCyc:6, TPCYC)
    TPREV(tpNameR:6, NAMEW)
    TPREV(tpTies:6, TPTIES)
    TPREV(conTab:011, CONWORDS)
    TPSINK(TPHDRWORDS)
    TPSINK(1)
tpDirRRuns,
    TPRUN(tpHdrB:6, TPHDRWORDS)
    TPRUN(tpDir:013, TPDIRW)
    TPRUN(tpEBuf:6, TPDIRREST)
    TPSINK(1)
tpDirWRuns,
    TPRUN(tpDHdr:6, TPHDRWORDS)
    TPRUN(tpDir:013, TPDIRW)
    TPZEROS(0d256 - TPHDRWORDS - TPDIRW)
    TPZEROS(1)

// The overlay's words, each set within the call that reads it, or assembled.
tpCyc,                  // the cycle's settings packed, as a save writes them and a load reads them
    table TPCYC, 0
tpZero, 0               // the word a save's padding repeats
tpSink, 0               // where a load's unkept words go
tpDirZ, 0               // the directory's block all zeros, a blank tape (tpRdDir)
tpOther, 0              // the directory's block another program's (tpRdDir)
tpOr, 0                 // the OR of the words read (tpOrN, tpScan)
tpW0, 0                 // the slot's first block's first data word (tpScan)
tpScB, 0                // the blocks tpScan reads, negative
tpScSt, 0               // the status at tpScan's stop
tpHdrA,                 // a load's leading header
    table TPHDRWORDS, 0
tpHdrB,                 // and its closing one, or the directory's
    table TPHDRWORDS, 0
tpDHdr,                 // the directory's header, as a save writes it
    TPMAGIC
    TPFORMAT
    TPDIRW
    0
    0
tpEntL,                 // an entry's tables' runs and its name's (tpEntRuns), then a 0
    table 3 * TPRECN + 3 + 1, 0
tpEBufL,                // an entry's run list on tape: tpEBuf, the padding, the closing
    table 3 * 3, 0
tpEBuf,                 // an entry's tables' words and its name, one after another (tpECopy)
    table MRECW + NAMEW, 0

// A master's record's tables, in an entry's order: each table's first word, the directory's
// table of counts, by master, that gives its words, and the count's multiplier.
tpRecT,
    mrWords:5; mLen:5; 1
    cpX:5; cpNP:5; 1
    cpY:5; cpNP:5; 1
    cpFrom:5; cpNL:5; 1
    cpTo:5; cpNL:5; 1
    cpC:5; cpNA:5; 1
    cpS:5; cpNA:5; 1
    cpE:5; cpNA:5; 1
    cpD:5; cpNA:5; 1
    cpK:5; cpNA:5; 1
    cpCon:5; cpNCon:011; CW
    cpSub:5; mNSub:5; SUBW
tpTies,                 // the tie lists packed, as a save writes them and a load reads them
    table TPTIES, 0
tpNameR,                // the name a load finds
    table NAMEW - 1, KBPAD
    KBBLANK

// Each picture's first block, P1 to P12, P7's after the directory's block.
tpFirst,
    1 + 0 * TPSLOT
    1 + 1 * TPSLOT
    1 + 2 * TPSLOT
    1 + 3 * TPSLOT
    1 + 4 * TPSLOT
    1 + 5 * TPSLOT
    TPDIRBLK + 1 + 0 * TPSLOT
    TPDIRBLK + 1 + 1 * TPSLOT
    TPDIRBLK + 1 + 2 * TPSLOT
    TPDIRBLK + 1 + 3 * TPSLOT
    TPDIRBLK + 1 + 4 * TPSLOT
    TPDIRBLK + 1 + 5 * TPSLOT

// Each picture's entry in tpDir, P1 to P12.
tpEntT,
    tpDir:013 + 0 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 1 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 2 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 3 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 4 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 5 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 6 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 7 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 0d8 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 0d9 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 0d10 * TPDENT
    tpDir:013 + 0d11 * TPDENT

// Save's keyboard prompt for each picture, P1 to P12, which tpPickNameOv sets in tpSvBlk.
tpPrmT,
    tpPrm1:013
    tpPrm2:013
    tpPrm3:013
    tpPrm4:013
    tpPrm5:013
    tpPrm6:013
    tpPrm7:013
    tpPrm8:013
    tpPrm9:013
    tpPrm10:013
    tpPrm11:013
    tpPrm12:013
%%endoverlay

// The tape's primitives, mount, seek, read and write, and their words, which every call sets
// before it reads them. They are root, in bank 11, since the overlays tape and library both
// call them; each is called via jsp i from W and returns across banks through rtn, which
// holds the caller's full address.

// Select the drive in use, wait out the selection delay, and learn whether it has a tape. A
// stop is refused, the error flag up, only when it has none (zsave.ac's test). A write-locked
// tape passes; a save to it fails at its write (tpWrite).
// Exit: AC = 0, or TSNOTAPE. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp i.
tpMount,
    local rtn, tmWait, tmNone, tmT0
    dac rtn
    lac i [tapeDrive:4]
    add [1]
    sal 6s
    sal 6s              // the unit, 1 to 8, in IO bits 2-5
    lia
    mse                 // clears any flag a previous operation left up
    rck
    dio tmT0
tmWait,
    rck
    lai
    sub tmT0
    spa                 // skip unless the clock wrapped
    add [0d60000]
    sub [TPSELMS]
    spa                 // skip once the delay has passed
    jmp tmWait
    cli
    mlc                 // stop, refused, the error flag up, with no tape
    mrs
    ril 2s              // the error flag to bit 0
    spi                 // skip if it is clear, a tape
    jmp tmNone
    cla
    jmp i rtn
tmNone,
    lac [TSNOTAPE]
    jmp i rtn
rtn, 0
tmT0, 0
    endloc

// Search to the flag of block tpWant, letting each flag steer (zsave.ac's zsvSeek). For a
// forward find (tpRev 0) the block's forward flag, for a reverse find (tpRev 1) its reverse
// flag. A forward flag past the block turns the tape back; one before it keeps it going, and so
// does one at it in a reverse find, which must pass the block before it turns. A reverse flag
// before the block turns it forward again; one past it keeps it reversing, and so does one at it
// in a forward find. The end zone turns it; a MISS is passed over.
// Entry: tpWant = the block and tpRev the direction, set by the caller, since jsp leaves its
// return in AC. Exit: AC = 0 as the flag arrives (the caller has 400 us to issue its mlc); TSBAD
// if the control refused (UNABLE), TSNOFLAG if no flag came in TPTMO polls, the tape still
// moving. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp i.
tpSeek,
    local rtn, tsArm, tsLoop, tsAt, tsRev, tsRAt, tsGoRev, tsGoFwd, tsNoDF, tsErr, tsIdle, \
        tsFail, tsN
    dac rtn
    lio [mtgo mtsrch]
    mlc
tsArm,
    lac [TPTMO]
    cma
    dac tpTmo
tsLoop,
    mrs
    spi i               // skip if the data flag is up, a flag's word
    jmp tsNoDF
    mrd
    dio tpWord
    lac tpWord
    and [mtblk]
    sub tpWant
    dac tsN             // n - want
    lio tpWord
    spi                 // skip if a forward flag
    jmp tsRev
    lac tsN
    sma                 // skip if before the block, to keep going
    jmp tsAt
    jmp tsArm
tsAt,
    sza                 // skip if at the block
    jmp tsGoRev         // past it, turn back
    lac tpRev
    sza i               // skip if a reverse find, to go on past the block, then turn
    jmp i rtn           // AC = 0, the block's forward flag
    jmp tsArm
tsRev,
    lac tsN
    spa                 // skip unless before the block, to turn forward
    jmp tsGoFwd
    sza                 // skip if at the block
    jmp tsArm           // past it, keep reversing
    lac tpRev
    sza                 // skip if a forward find, to keep reversing past the block
    jmp tsRAt
    jmp tsArm
tsRAt,
    cla
    jmp i rtn           // AC = 0, the block's reverse flag
tsGoFwd,
    lio [mtgo mtsrch]
    mlc
    jmp tsArm
tsGoRev,
    lio [mtgo mtrev mtsrch]
    mlc
    jmp tsArm
tsNoDF,
    ril 2s              // the error flag to bit 0
    spi i               // skip if it is up
    jmp tsIdle
    mrs
    dio tpStat
    lac tpStat
    and [mtend]
    sza i               // skip if the end zone
    jmp tsErr
    lac tpStat
    and [mtrevs]
    sza                 // skip if forward, at the far end zone
    jmp tsGoFwd
    jmp tsGoRev
tsErr,
    lac tpStat
    and [mtmiss]
    sza i               // skip if a MISS, to carry on
    jmp tsFail          // UNABLE, no tape, or off the reel
    lac tpStat
    and [mtrevs]
    sza                 // skip if forward; mlc clears the flag
    jmp tsGoRev
    jmp tsGoFwd
tsIdle,
    isp tpTmo
    jmp tsLoop
    lac [TSNOFLAG]
    jmp i rtn
tsFail,
    lac [TSBAD]
    jmp i rtn
rtn, 0
tsN, 0
    endloc

// Step to the next run of the list tpList points to: its first word, its count (stored
// complemented) and its step. The word loops take the next run inline, as this does.
// AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jsp.
tpNextRun,
    dap tnRtn
    lac i tpList
    dac tpAt
    idx tpList
    lac i tpList
    dac tpLeft
    idx tpList
    lac i tpList
    dac tpStep
    idx tpList
tnRtn, jmp .

// A block's start, 256 words to go, its sum zero.
// AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jsp.
tpBlock,
    dap tkRtn
    law i 0400
    dac tpWc
    dzm tpSum
tkRtn, jmp .

// Write -tpBlk blocks from the run list tpList points to, the seek having just found the first
// block's flag; each block's 256 words, then on its end the checksum, the complement of their
// sum. The tape is stopped after the last.
// Exit: AC = 0 (TSSAVED); TSLOCKED if the control refused the write (UNABLE, the drive
// write-locked); TSBAD on any other error. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp i.
tpWrite,
    local rtn, twData, tw1, twTail, twNoDF, twTNo, twBEF, twTmr, twNext, twErr, twWhy, twBad
    dac rtn
    jsp tpNextRun
    jsp tpBlock
    lio [mtgo mtwrit]
    mlc                 // the control asks for the first word at once
twData,
    mrs
    spi i               // skip if the data flag is up
    jmp twNoDF
    lio i tpAt
    mwr
    lai
    add tpSum
    dac tpSum
    lac tpAt
    add tpStep
    dac tpAt
    isp tpLeft
    jmp tw1
    lac i tpList        // the next run, inline (tpNextRun)
    dac tpAt
    idx tpList
    lac i tpList
    dac tpLeft
    idx tpList
    lac i tpList
    dac tpStep
    idx tpList
tw1,
    isp tpWc
    jmp twData
twTail,                 // the block's words all given, wait for its end
    mrs
    spi i
    jmp twTNo
    cli
    mwr                 // a word past 256 is never asked for; zero if it is
    jmp twTail
twNoDF,
    ril 1s              // the block end flag to bit 0, too soon here
    spi
    jmp twErr
    ril 1s              // the error flag to bit 0
    spi
    jmp twErr
    ril 4s              // GO (bit 6) to bit 0, clear after a halt, so no flag will come
    spi
    jmp twData
    jmp twErr
twTNo,
    ril 1s
    spi
    jmp twBEF
    ril 1s
    spi
    jmp twErr
    ril 4s
    spi
    jmp twTail
    jmp twErr
twBEF,
    lac tpSum
    cma
    lia
    mwr                 // the trailing checksum
    isp tpBlk
    jmp twNext
    law i 0d20          // about 300 us; the checksum reaches the tape 200 us after the flag
    dac tpTmo
twTmr,
    isp tpTmo
    jmp twTmr
    mrs
    dio tpStat
    cli
    mlc                 // stop
    lac tpStat
    and [mterf]
    sza i               // skip if a tape error
    jmp i rtn           // AC = 0
    jmp twWhy
twNext,
    jsp tpBlock
    jmp twData
twErr,
    mrs
    dio tpStat
    cli
    mlc                 // stop
twWhy,
    lac tpStat
    and [mtunab]
    sza i               // skip if UNABLE, the write refused
    jmp twBad
    lac [TSLOCKED]
    jmp i rtn
twBad,
    lac [TSBAD]
    jmp i rtn
rtn, 0
    endloc

// Read -tpBlk blocks into the run list tpList points to, the seek having just found the first
// block's flag. At tpRead going forward; at tpReadR in reverse, where a block gives its trailing
// checksum first, its words last first and its leading checksum last, so the list's runs walk
// backward (tpLoadRuns). Each block's two checksums and 256 words summed, and tpBad counting the
// blocks whose sum is not zero. The tape is stopped after the last.
// Exit: AC = 0, tpBad set; TSBAD on a tape error. IO is clobbered. Called via jsp i.
tpReadR,
    local rtn, trGo, trLead, trData, tr1, trTail, trLdNo, trNoDF, trTNo, trBEF, trNext, trErr
    dac rtn
    lio [mtgo mtread mtrev]
    jmp trGo
tpRead,
    dac rtn
    lio [mtgo mtread]
trGo,
    dzm tpBad
    jsp tpNextRun
    jsp tpBlock
    mlc
trLead,
    mrs
    spi i               // skip if the data flag is up
    jmp trLdNo
    mrd                 // the leading checksum, or in reverse the trailing one
    lai
    add tpSum
    dac tpSum
trData,
    mrs
    spi i
    jmp trNoDF
    mrd
    dio i tpAt
    lai
    add tpSum
    dac tpSum
    lac tpAt
    add tpStep
    dac tpAt
    isp tpLeft
    jmp tr1
    lac i tpList        // the next run, inline (tpNextRun)
    dac tpAt
    idx tpList
    lac i tpList
    dac tpLeft
    idx tpList
    lac i tpList
    dac tpStep
    idx tpList
tr1,
    isp tpWc
    jmp trData
trTail,                 // the block's words all taken, wait for its end
    mrs
    spi i
    jmp trTNo
    mrd                 // a word past 256 is never given; summed if it is
    lai
    add tpSum
    dac tpSum
    jmp trTail
trLdNo,
    ril 1s              // the block end flag to bit 0, too soon here
    spi
    jmp trErr
    ril 1s              // the error flag to bit 0
    spi
    jmp trErr
    ril 4s              // GO (bit 6) to bit 0
    spi
    jmp trLead
    jmp trErr
trNoDF,
    ril 1s
    spi
    jmp trErr
    ril 1s
    spi
    jmp trErr
    ril 4s
    spi
    jmp trData
    jmp trErr
trTNo,
    ril 1s
    spi
    jmp trBEF
    ril 1s
    spi
    jmp trErr
    ril 4s
    spi
    jmp trTail
    jmp trErr
trBEF,
    mrd                 // the trailing checksum, or in reverse the leading one
    lai
    add tpSum
    sza                 // skip if the block totals zero
    idx tpBad
    isp tpBlk
    jmp trNext
    mrs
    dio tpStat
    cli
    mlc                 // stop
    lac tpStat
    and [mterf]
    sza i               // skip if a tape error
    jmp i rtn           // AC = 0
    lac [TSBAD]
    jmp i rtn
trNext,
    jsp tpBlock
    jmp trLead
trErr,
    cli
    mlc                 // stop
    lac [TSBAD]
    jmp i rtn
rtn, 0
    endloc

tpWant, 0               // the block a seek wants
tpRev, 0                // 0 for a seek's forward find, 1 for a reverse find
tpWord, 0               // a flag's word
tpStat, 0               // the status at an error or a stop
tpTmo, 0                // a wait's count
tpList, 0               // the run list's next entry, a 16-bit pointer
tpAt, 0                 // the run's next word, a 16-bit pointer
tpLeft, 0               // the run's words to go, negative
tpStep, 0               // 1, -1 in the reverse pass, or 0 for a run of one word over and over
tpWc, 0                 // the block's words to go, negative
tpSum, 0                // the block's sum
tpBlk, 0                // the blocks to go, negative
tpBad, 0                // the blocks whose sum was not zero

// The main bank's two entries, root stubs calling the overlay's (tapeEntryOv, tpPickNameOv)
// through the drum overlay manager, which reads the overlay into W first if W holds another. IO
// passes through to the entry and AC comes back from it. While the
// overlay asks for a master's record (TSMORE), tapeEntry makes master tpK's record resident
// (the instance module's mrLoad, through mrLoadX) and calls it again with TEMORE. The library's
// entries, TELSAVE to TELDEL, and Plot's, TEPLOT, go on to the library's stub (splib.ac,
// libEntry).
// Entry and exit as the overlay's entry. Called via jsp i [tapeEntry:013] and
// jsp i [tpPickName:013], from the main bank.
tapeEntry,
    dac teStubR
    dio teArg
    lai
    sub [TELSAVE]
    sma                 // skip if one of the tape's entries
    jmp libEntry
teAgain,
    lio teArg
    %%ovcall tape, tapeEntryOv
    sas [TSMORE]        // skip if the overlay asks for master tpK's record
    jmp i teStubR
    lio tpK
    jsp i [mrLoadX:7]
    law TEMORE
    dac teArg
    jmp teAgain
tpPickName,
    dac pnStubR
    %%ovcall tape, tpPickNameOv
    jmp i pnStubR
teStubR, 0
teArg, 0
pnStubR, 0

// Misc's Save, Load and Dir rows and Library's, a step at a time, for the main bank's actTape,
// which does what each step asks: opens the keyboard on a block, or runs a tape entry through
// tapeCall and gives its result straight back. A row's first step is chosen by its item, tsItem;
// each later one is the step tsGo was aimed at, given the answer to the one before. Save and Load
// read the directory (TEDIR) and pick a picture on its screen (tpSvPick, tpLdPick), the one
// picked tapePic; Save then opens the keyboard on its name (tpPickName, tpSvBlk) and saves it at
// OK (TESAVE), and Load loads it (TELOAD). Dir reads the directory and shows it (tpDirBlk), its
// OK closing it with nothing more. A read that fails, a Cancel, or the result of the last entry
// ends the row (tsEnd). Library's rows are libStep's (splib.ac), which aims tsGo as these do,
// and Plot's is tsPlot's (spplot.ac), its entry TEPLOT.
// Entry: IO = TSFRESH for a row's first step, its item the main bank's lastItem; else the answer,
// the entry's result, or 1 for OK or a pick, 0 for Cancel. Exit: AC = 0 for nothing more, a
// block's 16-bit address for the keyboard, or a tape entry's number complemented. IO is
// clobbered. Called via jsp i [tapeStep:013], from the main bank.
tapeStep,
    local tsDir, tsPick, tsLoad, tsSvPk, tsSvOK, tsLdPk
    dac tsRtn
    dio tsAns
    lai
    sas [TSFRESH]       // skip if a row's first step
    jmp tsGo
    lac i [lastItem:4]
    dac tsItem
    sad [IPLOT]         // skip unless Plot's row
    jmp tsPlot
    sub [ILIB]
    sma                 // skip unless one of Library's rows
    jmp libStep
    law tsDir
    dap tsGo
    law i TEDIR
    jmp i tsRtn
tsGo, jmp .             // the step aimed at last

    // The directory read: Dir's screen, or Save's or Load's picker.
tsDir,
    lac tsAns
    sas [TSOPEN]        // skip if the read succeeded
    jmp tsEnd
    lac tsItem
    sas [IMISC + ROWDIR] // skip if Dir's row
    jmp tsPick
    lac [tpDirBlk:013]
    jmp i tsRtn
tsPick,
    sas [IMISC + ROWSAVE] // skip if Save's row
    jmp tsLoad
    law tsSvPk
    dap tsGo
    lac [tpSvPick:013]
    jmp i tsRtn
tsLoad,
    law tsLdPk
    dap tsGo
    lac [tpLdPick:013]
    jmp i tsRtn

    // Save's picker closed: a picture picked, the keyboard on its name.
tsSvPk,
    lac tsAns
    sza i               // skip if a picture was picked
    jmp tsEnd
    lac i [kbPick:6]
    dac i [tapePic:4]
    jsp tpPickName
    law tsSvOK
    dap tsGo
    lac [tpSvBlk:013]
    jmp i tsRtn

    // Save's keyboard closed: OK saves the picture under the name typed.
tsSvOK,
    lac tsAns
    sza i               // skip if OK
    jmp tsEnd
    law tsEnd
    dap tsGo
    law i TESAVE
    jmp i tsRtn

    // Load's picker closed: the picture picked is loaded.
tsLdPk,
    lac tsAns
    sza i               // skip if a picture was picked
    jmp tsEnd
    lac i [kbPick:6]
    dac i [tapePic:4]
    law tsEnd
    dap tsGo
    law i TELOAD
    jmp i tsRtn
    endloc

// Nothing more: the row's end.
tsEnd,
    cla
    jmp i tsRtn
tsRtn, 0                // the main bank's return
tsAns, 0                // the answer to the step before
tsItem, 0               // the row's item
